  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Norleucine and the PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. Norleucine is linked to the sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which is targeted by Artemisitene and 3-Methylenenorvaline, both of which ultimately act on CDC2L2. This indicates a possible pathway where Norleucine may influence the activity of these targets, which in turn modulate CDC2L2. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across different targets, but the specific molecular interactions and functional roles of Norleucine in this cascade are not fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on CDC2L2 supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Norleucine in the regulation of CDC2L2.",
